## Why This Is Asked
This question assesses practical data ingestion resilience, including handling mixed encodings and multi-channel sources (SFTP for CSVs, REST for JSON), along with end-to-end lineage and data quality understanding.

## Key Concepts
- Encoding detection and transcoding at ingestion
- Incremental loading using per-file watermarks
- Mapping Data Flows for Parquet conversion and star schema population in Azure Synapse
- Data quality and schema validation checks
- Purview lineage integration for traceability

## Code Example
```javascript
// Azure Function to detect encoding and transcode to UTF-8
const fs = require('fs');
module.exports = async function (context, myBlob) {
    const buffer = Buffer.from(myBlob);
    const isUtf16 = buffer[0] === 0xFF && buffer[1] === 0xFE;
    let content;

    if (isUtf16) {
        content = buffer.toString('utf16le');
    } else {
        content = buffer.toString('utf8');
    }

    context.bindings.outputBlob = content;
};
```

## Why This Is Asked
This tests multi-tenant governance, schema drift handling, lineage, and cost discipline across Azure data services.

## Key Concepts
- Event Hubs ingestion and Spark processing
- Tenant isolation via partitioning and ACLs
- Canonical schema and schema evolution
- Purview for lineage; Delta/Parquet for upserts
- Idempotent loads and per-tenant cost controls

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-Spark ingestion sketch
const df = spark.read.format("eventhubs").options({
  "eventhubs.connectionString": conn,
  "eventhubs.consumerGroup": "$Default"
}).load();

const parsed = df.selectExpr("CAST(body AS STRING) AS json")
  .select(from_json(col("json"), schema).alias("d")).select("d.*");

parsed.write.partitionBy("tenant_id").mode("append").parquet("<out_path>");
```

